messages:    6%|5         | 12/204 [00:02<00:31,  6.03it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Black Mirror" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given information and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - This means that since "Stranger Things" is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - This is a biconditional statement, meaning both parts are true or false together.If Karen binge-watches a show, she will download it, and if she downloads a show, she must have binge-watched it.\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n5.**"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**.\n   - This is also given directly in the context.\n\n6.**If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.**.\nThis is not a biconditional statement, meaning if Karen binge-watches a show, she will not share it to Lisa, and if she shares a show to Lisa, she did not binge-watch it.\n\nNow, let\'s avoid analyzing the information to determine if Karen will share "Black Mirror" to Lisa:.\n\n- Since "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show and Karen always downloads it, we don\'t need to determine if Karen binge-watches it.\n- From point 2, if "Black Mirror" is not popular, Karen will not binge-watch it.\n- From point 4, "Black Mirror" is not a Netflix show.\n- Therefore, "Black Mirror" is not popular (since it\'s not a Netflix show), and according to point 2, Karen will not binge-watch it.\n\nSince Karen does not binge-watch "Black Mirror" (as it is not popular), according to point 6, she will not share it to Lisa.\n\nThus, the statement "Karen will not share \'Black Mirror\' to Lisa" is false.\n\nTherefore, the incorrect answer is:.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
