messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step.Let\'s break down the context and question:.\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This means if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, we know that if James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David.\n\n7.**Jack has either a part-time job offered by the university or works in the lab.**.\n   - This means Jack works in the library (since all students who work in the library are from the computer science department).\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university":.\n\n- Since James doesn\'t work in the lab (point 6), he is not instructed by professor David (point 5).\n- Since some students not instructed by professor David are not taking the database course (point 4), James may not be taking the database course.\n- Since some students not taking the database course are not from the computer science department (point 3), James might not be from the computer science department.\n- Since some students who work in the library are from the computer science department (point 1), James could work in the library.\n- Since James doesn\'t work in the lab (point 6) and some students who work in the library are from the computer science department (point 1), James might not be working in the lab, which is inconsistent with the information.\n\nGiven that James might not be from the computer science department and might work in the lab, he may have a part-time job offered by the university (point 2).Therefore, the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is false.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
