messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step and see if we can derive a conclusion about James\' employment status.\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This implies that if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, we know that if James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David.\n\n7.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - Since James is instructed by professor David, he must be taking the database course.\n\n8.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - Since James is taking the database course, he must be from the computer science department.\n\n9.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - Since James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library.\n\n10.James doesn\'t work in the lab.\n    - Since James is working in the lab and he is from the computer science department, he can work in the library.\n\n11.**Jack has a part-time job offered by the university and also works in the lab.**.\n    - This information is crucial to James\' employment status.\n\nFrom the above analysis, we can conclude:.\n- James is not from the computer science department.\n- James is not working in the lab.\n- Since James is not from the computer science department, he can work in the library.\n- Since James is not working in the lab, he is not instructed by professor David.\n- Since James is not instructed by professor David, he is not taking the database course.\n- Since James is not taking the database course, he is not from the computer science department.\n- Since James is not from the computer science department, he can work in the library.\n- Since James is not working in the lab, he can have a part-time job offered by the university (because students who work in the library are not from the computer science department).\n\nTherefore, the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
