messages:   21%|##1       | 43/204 [00:09<00:24,  6.45it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf a man is taller than another man, the taller one can block the other's shooting. Michael is a man who is taller than everyone else in his class. If person x is taller than person y, and person y is taller than person z, than x is taller than z Peter is a man who is taller than Michael. Michael can block any shooting from a person as long as the person does not jump when shooting. Michael cannot block Windy's shooting. Every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Windy is a great shooter.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Windy is a great shooter" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**Michael\'s Height and Blocking Ability**:.\n   - Michael is taller than everyone in his class.\n   - Michael can block any shooting from a person as long as the person does not jump when shooting.\n\n2.**Peter\'s Height**:.\n   - Peter is taller than Michael.\n\n3.**Michael\'s Blocking Condition**:.\n   - Michael cannot block Windy\'s shooting.\n\n4.**Jumping and Great Shooter**:.\n   - Every shooter who can jump when shooting is a great shooter.\n\nFrom the information provided, we know:.\n- Michael is taller than Peter.\n- Michael cannot block Windy\'s shooting.\nWindy is not a great shooter, as Michael can easily block Windy\'s shooting. Windy\'s inability to jump when shooting indicates a lack of skill, contrary to the belief that great shooters can jump when shooting.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
