is implies that if an employee is in another country, they are working remotely from home.\n\n6.**No managers work remotely from home.**.\n   - This means if an employee is a manager, they must be in the company today.\n\n7.**James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.**.\n   - This gives us two possible scenarios for James:.\n     - Scenario 1: James is a manager and appears in the company today.\n     - Scenario 2: James is not a manager and does not appear in the company today.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each scenario:.\n\nJames has lunch in the company.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
