messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition. If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus. People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls. If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze the statement step by step.We need to determine if the statement "Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls" is true, false, or uncertain based on the provided information.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - If people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition.\n   - If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus.\n   - People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.\n   - If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.\n   - If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n   - Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n2.**Statement to Evaluate:**.\n   - Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\n3.**Logical Steps:**.\n   - From the context, we know Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n   - Since Mary works in student jobs on campus, she must order takeout frequently (from the context "If people work in student jobs on campus, then they order takeout frequently in college").\nSince Mary is a picky eater and does not spend a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls, the statement "Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls" is false.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
