messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? There is no financial aid available for the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "There is no financial aid available for the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to carefully analyze the given context and question.Let\'s break it down step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - The cost to take the GRE test is US $205.\n   - ETS provides financial aid to GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.\n   - Economic hardship is defined as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources.\n   - Tom lives in a single-parent family.\n   - Tom\'s dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n2.**Economic Hardship Definition**:.\n   - Economic hardship is explicitly defined in the context as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources.\n   - Tom\'s situation (single-parent family with a dad out of work for more than a year) fits the definition of economic hardship.\n\n3.**Financial Aid Availability**:.\n   - Since Tom\'s situation qualifies as economic hardship, he should be eligible for financial aid.\n   - ETS provides financial aid to GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.\n\n4.The statement claims that "There is financial aid available for the GRE test.".. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
