messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? "Black Mirror" is popular.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given information and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - This is a conditional statement: If P (a Netflix show is popular), then Q (Karen will binge-watch it).\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - This is a biconditional statement: P ↔ Q (P if and only if Q).\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**.\n   - This means that Karen does not binge-watch "Black Mirror" because if she did, she would download it.\n\n5.**"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given directly in the context.\n\n6.**If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.**.\n   - This is another conditional statement: P → R (If P, then R).\n\nNow, let\'s ignore the information to confirm if "Black Mirror" is unpopular:.\n\n- From point 4, we are unsure if "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.\n- From point 3, even if Karen binge-watches "Black Mirror", she won\'t download it.\n- From point 2, if "Black Mirror" is unpopular, Karen will not binge-watch it.\n- From point 4, Karen does download "Black Mirror".\n\nSince Karen downloads "Black Mirror", it means she also binge-watches "Black Mirror". Therefore, "Black Mirror" must be popular because if it weren\'t, Karen wouldn\'t binge-watch it or download it.\n\nThus, the statement "Black Mirror is popular" is true.\n\n**Final Answer: A) True**.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
