messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can derive a conclusion about Luke\'s behavior regarding his siblings.\n1.**Condition 1:** If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.\n   - This implies that if Luke is a twin or triplet, he spends a lot of time with his siblings.\n2.**Condition 2:** If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.\n   - This is a restatement of Condition 1, so it doesn\'t provide new information.\n3.**Condition 3:** If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.\n   - This implies that if Luke complains often about annoying siblings, he has siblings who are the same age.\n4.**Condition 4:** If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.\n   - This implies that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he does not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n5.**Condition 5:** If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.\n   - This implies that if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he often did not live at home regularly.\n6.**Given Information:** Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n   - This gives us two possible scenarios:\n     a) Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members.\n     b) Luke is neither a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n7.**Analysis:**\n   - If Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members (Scenario a), then he must not live at home regularly (Condition 4).\n   - If Luke does not live at home regularly (Condition 4), then he often did not spend a lot of time with his siblings (Condition 5).The statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is true.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
