messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInternational students in US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa. An international student in US with an F1 visa needs to apply for CPT or OPT if the student wants to work in the US. Mike is an international student. Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mike has a J1 visa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - International students in the US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa.\n   - An international student with an F1 visa needs to apply for CPT or OPT if they want to work in the US.\n   - Mike is an international student.\n   - Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n\n2.**Key Points**:.\n   - Mike is an international student.\n   - Mike needs to apply for CPT if he wants to work in the US.\n   - The context specifies that international students in the US have either an F1 visa or a J1 visa.\n\n3.**Implications**:.\n   - Since Mike needs to apply for CPT, it implies that he is not already working in the US (as CPT is for students who want to work in the US).\n   - Therefore, Mike must be in a situation where he is not working in the US and needs to apply for CPT.\n\nMike does not have a J1 visa, so the statement "Mike has an F1 visa" is certain.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
