messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition. If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus. People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls. If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine the truth of the statement "Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls," we need to analyze the given context step by step and see if we can derive the necessary conditions for the statement to be true.\n\n1.**Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.**.\n   - This is given in the context, so we know this part is true.\n\n2.**If people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition.**.\n   - This is a conditional statement that is true based on the context.\n\n3.**If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus.**.\n   - This is another conditional statement.However, we don\'t have information about whether Mary orders takeout frequently or not.\n\n4.**People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.**.\n   - This is a disjunction.We need to determine which of these two options Mary falls under.\n\n5.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.**.\n   - This is a conditional statement.If Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, then she is not picky.\n\n6.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.**.\n   - This is another conditional statement.If Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\n7.**If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.**.\nMary is a picky eater and does not spend a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
