messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to carefully analyze the given context and question.Let\'s break it down step by step:\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:\n   - The cost to take the GRE test is explicitly stated as US $205.\n   - ETS provides financial aid to GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.\n   - Tom\'s family situation is described: he lives in a single-parent family, and his dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n2.**Question Analysis**:\n   - We need to determine if the cost of the GRE test is below US $300.\n\n3.**Cost Comparison**:\n   - The cost of the GRE test is US $205.\n   - We need to compare this cost to US $300.\n\n4.**Logical Reasoning**:\n   - Since US $205 is greater than US $300, the statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test" is false.\n\n5.**Conclusion**:\n   - Given that the cost of the GRE test is US $205, which is indeed above US $300, the statement is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n<answer>B) False</answer>\n</think>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
