any financial aid.\n\nGiven this context, Tom's situation, with his dad being out of work for more than a year, strongly suggests that he would be eligible for financial aid. However, the exact amount of aid he receives would depend on the specific financial need assessment and the availability of funds.\n\nIn conclusion, while Tom's situation indicates a high likelihood of qualifying for financial aid, the final determination would be based on the documentation he provides and the assessment by ETS. Therefore, the statement \"It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test\" is false, as the cost is US $205, which is below US $300.\n</think>\n<answer>B) False</answer>\n</answer>",
