messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people perform in school talent shows often, then they attend and are very engaged with school events. People either perform in school talent shows often or are inactive and disinterested members of their community. If people chaperone high school dances, then they are not students who attend the school. All people who are inactive and disinterested members of their community chaperone high school dances. All young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school. Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If Bonnie either chaperones high school dances or, if she does not, she performs in school talent shows often, then Bonnie is both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze the statement step by step.We need to determine if the statement "If Bonnie either chaperones high school dances or, if she does not, she performs in school talent shows often, then Bonnie is both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and an inactive and disinterested member of the community" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - If people perform in school talent shows often, then they attend and are very engaged with school events.\n   - People either perform in school talent shows often or are inactive and disinterested members of their community.\n   - If people chaperone high school dances, then they are not students who attend the school.\n   - All people who are inactive and disinterested members of their community chaperone high school dances.\n   - All young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school.\n   - Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\n2.**Statement to Evaluate:**.\n   - If Bonnie either chaperones high school dances or, if she does not, she performs in school talent shows often, then Bonnie is both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n\n3.**Logical Breakdown:**.\n   - Let\'s denote:.\n     - \\( P \\): Bonnie performs in school talent shows often.\n     - \\( Q \\): Bonnie chaperones high school dances.\n     - \\( R \\): Bonnie is a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities.\n     - \\( S \\): Bonnie is an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n\n   - The given statement can be written as:.\n     \\[.\n     (Q \\lor \\neg P) \\rightarrow (R \\land S).\n     \\].\n\n4.**Analyze the Conditions:**.\n   - From the context, we know:.\n     - If Bonnie performs in school talent shows often (\\( P \\)), then she attends and is very engaged with school events.\n     - If Bonnie attends and is very engaged with school events, then she is a student who attends the school.\n     - If Bonnie is a student who attends the school, then she is a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities (\\( R \\)).\n     - If Bonnie is a student who attends the school, then she is not an inactive and disinterested member of the community (\\( \\neg S \\)).\n     - If Bonnie chaperones high school dances (\\( Q \\)), then she is not a student who attends the school.\n     - If Bonnie is not a student who attends the school, then she is an inactive and disinterested member of the community (\\( S \\)).The statement is false in all invalid scenarios, which contradicts the given conditions. Therefore, the statement is only true if Bonnie does not perform in school talent shows often.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 84%|########4 | 172/204 [05:28<00:03,  8.47it/s]
